  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Introduced in\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Strixhaven: A Curriculum of Chaos",
              "href": "https://www.amazon.com/Strixhaven-Curriculum-Adventure-Dungeons-Dragons/dp/0786967447?crid=2IP1T7Y1EYAP9&keywords=strixhaven+d%26d+book&qid=1639062297&sprefix=strixha%2Caps%2C221&sr=8-1-spons&psc=1&spLa=ZW5jcnlwdGVkUXVhbGlmaWVyPUExVU5YSjRLOTU0Q002JmVuY3J5cHRlZElkPUEwMDU0NjE4MTIySVhHQlRRTE9aQiZlbmNyeXB0ZWRBZElkPUEwNzIwNTgxMVRDT1FCRFNHOFlSNyZ3aWRnZXROYW1lPXNwX2F0ZiZhY3Rpb249Y2xpY2tSZWRpcmVjdCZkb05vdExvZ0NsaWNrPXRydWU%3D&linkCode=ll1&tag=rpgbot-20&linkId=c65f57f7288786ee94aeb958f2170adc&language=en_US&ref_=as_li_ss_tl"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\t("
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "affiliate link",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/about/faq/#what-are-affiliate-links-and-why-do-you-use-them"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "), the Owlin is an owl-like humanoid. Similar to the Aarakocra, the Owlin can\n\tfly nonmagically, but the Owlin trades a bit of the Aarakocra’s speed and the\n\tAarakocra’s largely useless claws for several other useful racial traits. The\n\tOwlin also benefits from the post-Tasha’s changes to race design, so much like\n\tthe lineages introduced in Van Richten’s Guide to Ravenloft and the Fairy,\n\tintroduced in The Wild beyond the Witchlight, the Owlin has their choice of\n\t+2/+1 increases or three +1 increases. Taken as a whole, the Owlin is outright\n\tbetter than the Aarakocra in everything except speed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Owlin also receive proficiency in Stealth. You may be locked into this choice since the Owlin doesn’t explicitly have the “Ability Score Increase” trait which is required to use the custom origin rules ("
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "see the Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything errata",
              "href": "https://media.wizards.com/2021/dnd/downloads/TCE-Errata.pdf"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ")."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
